<title>FRANCE: Moroccan firms buy feed barley, probably Spanish.</title>
<headline>Moroccan firms buy feed barley, probably Spanish.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Private Moroccan importers on Thursday bought over 10,000 tonnes of European Union feed barley for spot delivery at around $132 per tonne, Fob, grain exporters said.</p>
<p>Traders said that pricing details suggested Spain was the most likely origin for the barley.</p>
<p>One exporter put the purchase at 16,000 tonnes while others said it covered more than 10,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
